window.RECALL_STARTER_REVIEWER = {"id":"reviewer-s2-it0015","title":"S2 It0015 - Clean Reviewer","questions":[{"sourceNumber":"1","text":"When the show spanning-tree vlan 33 command is issued on a switch, three ports are shown in\nthe forwarding state. In which port role could these interfaces function while in the forwarding\nstate?","options":["alternate","designated","blocked","disabled"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"2","text":"Which statement describes a characteristic of EtherChannel?","options":["It can combine up to a maximum of 4 physical links.","It consists of multiple parallel links","It is made by combining multiple physical links that are seen as one link","It can bundle mixed types of 100 Mb/s and 1Gb/s Ethernet links."],"correctAnswers":[2],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"3","text":"Your switch has a port status LED that is alternating between green and amber. What could this\nindicate?","options":["The port is in STP blocking mode.","The port is experiencing errors.","Nothing; this is normal","The port is shut down"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"4","text":"Which protocol provides up to 16 instances of RSTP, combines many VLANs with the same\nphysical and logical topology into a common RSTP instance, and provides support for PortFast,\nBPDU guard, BPDU filter, root guard, and loop guard?","options":["PVST+","Rapid PVST+","MST","STP"],"correctAnswers":[2],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"5","text":"Which one is an advantage of EtherChannel?","options":["Spanning Tree Protocol ensures redundancy by transitioning failed interfaces in an EtherChannel to a\nforwarding state.","Load balancing occurs","Configuring the EtherChannel interface provides consistency in the configuration of the\nphysical links.","EtherChannel uses upgraded physical links to provide increased bandwidth."],"correctAnswers":[2],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"6","text":"Refer to the exhibit. A network administrator is configuring an EtherChannel link between two\nswitches, SW1 and SW2. However, the EtherChannel link fails to establish. What change in\nconfiguration would correct the problem?","options":["Configure SW2 EtherChannel mode to desirable.","Configure SW2 EtherChannel mode to auto.","Configure SW2 EtherChannel mode to on.","Configure SW1 EtherChannel mode to on."],"correctAnswers":[0],"images":["data:image/png;base64,"],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"7","text":"A small company network has six interconnected Layer 2 switches. Currently all switches are\nusing the default bridge priority value. Which value can be used to configure the bridge priority\nof one of the switches to ensure that it becomes the root bridge in this design?","options":["28672","32768","34816","1"],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"8","text":"Which one is load-balancing method in the EtherChannel technology?","options":["source IP to destination IP","combination of source port and IP to destination port and IP","combination of source MAC and IP to destination MAC and IP","source port to destination port"],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"9","text":"What is a drawback to turning spanning tree off and having multiple paths through the Layer 2\nswitch network?","options":["Port security becomes unstable.","The switch acts like a hub.","Broadcast frames are transmitted indefinitely.","Port security shuts down all of the ports that have attached devices."],"correctAnswers":[2],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"10","text":"When EtherChannel is configured, which mode will force an interface into a port channel without\nexchanging aggregation protocol packets?","options":["active","on","auto","desirable"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"11","text":"What one is a requirement to be able to configure an EtherChannel between two switches?","options":["All the interfaces need to work at the same speed.","Different allowed ranges of VLANs must exist on each end.","All interfaces need to be assigned to different VLANs.","The interfaces that are involved need to be contiguous on the switch."],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"12","text":"Refer to the exhibit. An EtherChannel was configured between switches S1 and S2, but the\ninterfaces do not form an EtherChannel. What is the problem?","options":["The EtherChannel was not configured with the same allowed range of VLANs on each\ninterface.","The switch ports have to be configured as access ports with each port having a VLAN assigned.","The interface port-channel number has to be different on each switch.","The switch ports were not configured with speed and duplex mode."],"correctAnswers":[0],"images":["data:image/png;base64,"],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"13","text":"What is the purpose of the Spanning Tree Protocol (STP)?","options":["prevents routing loops on a router","creates smaller collision domains","prevents Layer 2 loops","creates smaller broadcast domains"],"correctAnswers":[2],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"14","text":"Which statement is true regarding the use of PAgP to create EtherChannels?","options":["It requires full duplex.","It requires more physical links than LACP does.","It is Cisco proprietary.","It increases the number of ports that are participating in spanning tree."],"correctAnswers":[2],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"15","text":"If no bridge priority is configured in PVST, which criteria is considered when electing the root\nbridge?","options":["highest MAC address","highest IP address","lowest IP address","lowest MAC address"],"correctAnswers":[3],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"16","text":"Refer to the exhibit. Which switching technology would allow each access layer switch link to be\naggregated to provide more bandwidth between each Layer 2 switch and the Layer 3 switch?","options":["HSRP","trunking","EtherChannel","PortFast"],"correctAnswers":[2],"images":["data:image/png;base64,"],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"17","text":"Which mode configuration setting would allow formation of an EtherChannel link between\nswitches SW1 and SW2 without sending negotiation traffic?","options":["SW1: on SW2: on SW1: on SW2: on","SW1: auto SW2: auto trunking enabled on both switches SW1: auto SW2: auto trunking enabled on\nboth switches","SW1: desirable SW2: desirable SW1: desirable SW2: desirable","SW1: auto SW2: auto PortFast enabled on both switches SW1: auto SW2: auto PortFast enabled on\nboth switches"],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"18","text":"Which one is an advantage of using LACP?","options":["It decreases the amount of configuration that is needed on a switch","It eliminates the need for configuring trunk interfaces when deploying VLANs on multiple switches.","LACP allows Fast Ethernet and Gigabit Ethernet interfaces to be mixed within a single EtherChannel.","It allows the use of multivendor devices."],"correctAnswers":[3],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"19","text":"Which one is a component of a bridge ID?","options":["extended system ID","bridge priority","IP address","port ID"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"20","text":"Which one is load-balancing method in the EtherChannel technology","options":["source MAC to destination MAC","source port to destination port","combination of source MAC and IP to destination MAC and IP","combination of source port and IP to destination port and IP"],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"21","text":"When a range of ports is being configured for EtherChannel, which mode will configure PAgP so\nthat it initiates the EtherChannel negotiation?","options":["Passive","Desirable","Auto","Active"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"22","text":"It is the Proprietary per VLAN implementation of IEEE 802.1w","options":["MSTP","RSTP","PVST+","RAPID PVST+"],"correctAnswers":[3],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"23","text":"What is a requirement to configure a trunking EtherChannel between two switches?","options":["The participating interfaces must be assigned the same VLAN number on both switches","The participating interfaces must be on the same module on a switch.","The participating interfaces must be physically contiguous on a switch.","The allowed range of VLANs must be the same on both switches."],"correctAnswers":[3],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"24","text":"Refer to the exhibit. A network administrator issued the show etherchannel summary command\non the switch S1. What conclusion can be drawn?","options":["The EtherChannel is suspended.","The port aggregation protocol PAgP is misconfigured.","The EtherChannel is not functional.","FastEthernet ports Fa0/1, Fa0/2, and Fa0/3 do not join the EtherChannel."],"correctAnswers":[2],"images":["data:image/png;base64,"],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"25","text":"Which spanning tree standard supports only one root bridge so that traffic from all VLANs flows\nover the same path?","options":["MST","802.1D","Rapid PVST","PVST+"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"26","text":"What is a characteristic of spanning tree?","options":["It is enabled by default on Cisco switches.","It has a TTL mechanism that works at Layer 2.","It prevents propagation of Layer 2 broadcast frames.","It is used to discover information about an adjacent Cisco device."],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"27","text":"Which protocol is used to implement EtherChannel?","options":["Port Aggregation Protocol","Cisco Discovery Protocol","Rapid Spanning Tree Protocol","Spanning Tree Protocol"],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"28","text":"A switch is configured to run STP. What term describes a non-root port that is permitted to\nforward traffic on the network?","options":["dedicated port","designated port","disabled","alternate port"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"29","text":"A switch is configured to run STP. What term describes a field used to specify a VLAN ID?","options":["extended system ID","bridge ID","bridge priority","port ID"],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"30","text":"Refer to the exhibit. While troubleshooting a switch, you executed the “show interface\nport-channel 1 etherchannel” command and it returned this output.​\nWhich information is provided by the Load value?","options":["the session count of the link","the preference of the link","the number source-destination pairs on the link","the percentage of use of the link"],"correctAnswers":[2],"images":["data:image/png;base64,"],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"31","text":"Which settings must match on both sides of the switch ports to form an EtherChannel?","options":["Only the switch port numbers must match","vlans & SNMP community strings should match","Interface speed, duplex & vlan should match","Only the SNMP community strings must match"],"correctAnswers":[2],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"32","text":"Rapid PVST+ is___________.","options":["An evolution of STP that provides faster convergence","A protocol that allows multiple VLANs to run in a single spanning-tree instance","The legacy standard for STP that runs all VLANs in a single spanning-tree instance.","A Cisco enhancement of RSTP to provide a spanning-tree instance for each VLAN"],"correctAnswers":[3],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"33","text":"What is the result of entering the command “port-channel load-balance src-dst-ip” on an\nEtherChannel link?","options":["Packets are distributed across the ports in the channel based on both the source and destination MAC\naddresses.","Packets are balanced across the ports in the channel based first on the source MAC address, then on\nthe destination MAC address, then on the IP address.","Packets are distributed across the ports in the channel based on both the source and\ndestination IP addresses.","Packets are distributed across the access ports in the channel based first on the source IP address and\nthen the destination IP addresses."],"correctAnswers":[2],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"34","text":"Refer to the exhibit. The administrator tried to create an EtherChannel between S1 and the\nother two switches via the commands that are shown, but was unsuccessful. What is the\nproblem?","options":["Traffic can only be sent to two different switches if EtherChannel is implemented on Gigabit Ethernet\ninterfaces.","Traffic can only be sent to two different switches if EtherChannel is implemented on Layer 3 switches.","Traffic cannot be sent to two different switches through the same EtherChannel link.","Traffic cannot be sent to two different switches, but only to two different devices like an\nEtherChannel-enabled server and a switch."],"correctAnswers":[2],"images":["data:image/png;base64,"],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"35","text":"Which mode is in PAgP?","options":["Auto","Active","Passive","On"],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"36","text":"Which one parameter must match on the ports of two switches to create a PAgP EtherChannel\nbetween the switches?","options":["VLAN information","MAC address","PAgP mode","port ID"],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"37","text":"IEEE standard that reduces the number of STP instances","options":["RAPID PVST+","MSTP","RSTP","PVST+"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"38","text":"What is the outcome of a Layer 2 broadcast storm?","options":["ARP broadcast requests are returned to the transmitting host.","New traffic is discarded by the switch because it is unable to be processed.","CSMA/CD will cause each host to continue transmitting frames.","Routers will take over the forwarding of frames as switches become congested."],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"39","text":"Which one is a network design feature that requires Spanning Tree Protocol (STP) to ensure\ncorrect network operation?","options":["link-state dynamic routing that provides redundant routes","implementing VLANs to contain broadcasts","static default routes","redundant links"],"correctAnswers":[3],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"40","text":"You have two switches connected together with two crossover cables for redundancy, and STP\nis disabled. Which of the following will happen between the switches?","options":["The switches will automatically load-balance","The MAC forward/filter table will not update on the switch.","Broadcast storms will occur on the switched network.","The routing tables on the switches will not update."],"correctAnswers":[2],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"41","text":"A network administrator has configured an EtherChannel between two switches that are\nconnected via four trunk links. If the physical interface for one of the trunk links changes to a\ndown state, what happens to the EtherChannel?","options":["The EtherChannel will transition to a down state.","Spanning Tree Protocol will transition the failed physical interface into forwarding mode.","Spanning Tree Protocol will recalculate the remaining trunk links.","The EtherChannel will remain functional."],"correctAnswers":[3],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"42","text":"A switch is configured to run STP. What term describes a field that has a default value of 32,768\nand is the initial deciding factor when electing a root bridge?","options":["bridge ID","bridge priority","extended system ID","MAC Address"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"43","text":"Refer to the exhibit. What are the possible port roles for ports A, B, C, and D in this\nRSTP-enabled network?","options":["designated, alternate, root, root","designated, root, alternate, root","alternate, designated, root, root","alternate, root, designated, root"],"correctAnswers":[2],"images":["data:image/png;base64,"],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"44","text":"A network administrator configured an EtherChannel link with three interfaces between two\nswitches. What is the result if one of the three interfaces is down?","options":["One interface becomes an active link for data traffic and the other becomes a backup link.","The remaining two interfaces become separate links","The remaining two interfaces continue to load balance traffic.","The EtherChannel fails."],"correctAnswers":[2],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"45","text":"The following configuration are used to configure stateless DHCPv6 Client on a Router.​\nR(config)# ipv6 unicast-routing​\nR(config-if)#ipv6 enable​\nR(config-if)#ipv6 address autoconfig","options":["True","False"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"boolean"},{"sourceNumber":"46","text":"A company uses DHCP servers to dynamically assign IPv4 addresses to employee\nworkstations. The address lease duration is set as 5 days. An employee returns to the office\nafter an absence of one week. When the employee boots the workstation, it sends a message\nto obtain an IP address. Which Layer 2 and Layer 3 destination addresses will the message\ncontain?","options":["both MAC and IPv4 addresses of the DHCP server","FF-FF-FF-FF-FF-FF and 255.255.255.255","MAC address of the DHCP server and 255.255.255.255","FF-FF-FF-FF-FF-FF and IPv4 address of the DHCP server"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"47","text":"The A flag signifies to use a stateful DHCPv6 server to obtain an IPv6 Global Unicast Address.","options":["True","False"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"boolean"},{"sourceNumber":"48","text":"Refer to the exhibit. A network administrator is implementing stateful DHCPv6 operation for the\ncompany. However, the clients are not using the prefix and prefix-length information that is\nconfigured in the DHCP pool. The administrator issues a show ipv6 interface command. What\ncould be the cause of the problem?","options":["The router is configured for SLAAC DHCPv6 operation","The router is configured for stateless DHCPv6 operation","The Duplicate Address Detection feature is disabled","No virtual link-local address is configured"],"correctAnswers":[1],"images":["data:image/png;base64,"],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"49","text":"Which set of commands will configure a router as a DHCP server that will assign IPv4\naddresses to the 192.168.100.0/23 LAN while reserving the first 10 and the last addresses for\nstatic assignment?","options":["ip dhcp excluded-address 192.168.100.1 192.168.100.10 ip dhcp excluded-address 192.168.100.254 ip\ndhcp pool LAN-POOL-100 network 192.168.100.0 255.255.255.0 ip default-gateway 192.168.100.1 ip\ndhcp excluded-address 192.168.100.1 192.168.100.10 ip dhcp excluded-address 192.168.100.254 ip\ndhcp pool LAN-POOL-100 network 192.168.100.0 255.255.255.0 ip default-gateway 192.168.100.1","dhcp pool LAN-POOL-100 ip dhcp excluded-address 192.168.100.1 192.168.100.9 ip dhcp\nexcluded-address 192.168.100.254 network 192.168.100.0 255.255.254.0 default-router 192.168.101.1\ndhcp pool LAN-POOL-100 ip dhcp excluded-address 192.168.100.1 192.168.100.9 ip dhcp\nexcluded-address 192.168.100.254 network 192.168.100.0 255.255.254.0 default-router 192.168.101.1","ip dhcp excluded-address 192.168.100.1 192.168.100.10 ip dhcp excluded-address\n192.168.101.254 ip dhcp pool LAN-POOL-100 network 192.168.100.0 255.255.254.0 default-router\n192.168.100.1 ip dhcp excluded-address 192.168.100.1 192.168.100.10 ip dhcp excluded-address\n192.168.101.254 ip dhcp pool LAN-POOL-100 network 192.168.100.0 255.255.254.0 default-router\n192.168.100.1","ip dhcp excluded-address 192.168.100.1 192.168.100.9 ip dhcp excluded-address 192.168.101.254 ip\ndhcp pool LAN-POOL-100 ip network 192.168.100.0 255.255.254.0 ip default-gateway 192.168.100.1\nip dhcp excluded-address 192.168.100.1 192.168.100.9 ip dhcp excluded-address 192.168.101.254 ip\ndhcp pool LAN-POOL-100 ip network 192.168.100.0 255.255.254.0 ip default-gateway 192.168.100.1"],"correctAnswers":[2],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"50","text":"The O flag signifies to use a stateful DHCPv6 server to obtain an IPv6 Global Unicast Address.","options":["True","False"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"boolean"},{"sourceNumber":"51","text":"The M flag signifies that additional information is available from a stateless DHCPv6 server","options":["True","False"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"boolean"},{"sourceNumber":"52","text":"A network administrator is analyzing the features that are supported by different first-hop router\nredundancy protocols. Which statement describes a feature that is associated with HSRP?","options":["HSRP is nonproprietary.","It allows load balancing","It uses ICMP messages in order to assign the default gateway to hosts.","HSRP uses active and standby routers."],"correctAnswers":[3],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"53","text":"Which address does a DHCPv4 server target when sending a DHCPOFFER message to a\nclient that makes an address request?","options":["client hardware address","gateway IP address","broadcast MAC address","client IP address"],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"54","text":"Refer to the exhibit. A network administrator is implementing the stateless DHCPv6 operation\nfor the company. Clients are configuring IPv6 addresses as expected. However, the clients are\nnot getting the DNS server address and the domain name information configured in the DHCP\npool. What could be the cause of the problem?","options":["The clients cannot communicate with the DHCPv6 server, evidenced by the number of active clients\nbeing 0.","The DNS server address is not on the same network as the clients are on.","The GigabitEthernet interface is not activated.","The router is configured for SLAAC operation."],"correctAnswers":[3],"images":["data:image/png;base64,"],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"55","text":"The address pool of a DHCP server is configured with 10.19.44.0/24. The network administrator\nreserves 6 IP addresses for servers. How many IP addresses are left in the pool to be assigned\nto other hosts?","options":["246","238","248","252"],"correctAnswers":[2],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"56","text":"The address pool of a DHCP server is configured with 10.7.30.0/24. The network administrator\nreserves 5 IP addresses for printers. How many IP addresses are left in the pool to be assigned\nto other hosts?","options":["247","249","239","253"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"57","text":"A client device on an Ethernet segment needs an IP address in order to communicate on the\nnetwork. A DHCP server with IP address 192.168.1.1 has been configured and enabled on the\nnetwork. How will a client device obtain a usable IP address for this network?","options":["Send a DHCPDISCOVER message to physical address FF-FF-FF-FF-FF-FF.","Send a DHCPREQUEST packet to IP address 255.255.255.255.","Send a DHCPACK packet to the default gateway address.","Use a statically configured IP address from the pool of IP addresses that is offered by the DHCP server."],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"58","text":"A company uses DHCP to manage IP address deployment for employee workstations. The IT\ndepartment deploys multiple DHCP servers in the data center and uses DHCP relay agents to\nfacilitate the DHCP requests from workstations. Which one UDP port is used to forward DHCP\ntraffic?","options":["67","68","53","23"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"59","text":"What information can be verified through the show ip dhcp binding command?","options":["that DHCPv4 discover messages are still being received by the DHCP server","the IPv4 addresses that have been excluded from the DHCPv4 pool","the number of IP addresses remaining in the DHCP pool","the IPv4 addresses that are assigned to hosts by the DHCP server"],"correctAnswers":[3],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"60","text":"Which command, when issued in the interface configuration mode of a router, enables the\ninterface to acquire an IPv4 address automatically from an ISP, when that link to the ISP is\nenabled?","options":["ip helper-address","service dhcp","ip dhcp pool","ip address dhcp"],"correctAnswers":[3],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"61","text":"What is a result when the DHCP servers are not operational in a network?","options":["Workstations are assigned with IP addresses in the 10.0.0.0/8 network.","Workstations are assigned with the IP address 127.0.0.1.","Workstations are assigned with the IP address 0.0.0.0.","Workstations are assigned with IP addresses in the 169.254.0.0/16 network."],"correctAnswers":[3],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"62","text":"Which protocol automates assignment of IP addresses on a network, and which port number\ndoes it use?","options":["DNS","SMB","80","DHCP"],"correctAnswers":[3],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"63","text":"What is the result of a network technician issuing the command ip dhcp excluded-address\n10.0.15.1 10.0.15.15 on a Cisco router?","options":["The ip dhcp excluded-address command is followed by the first and the last addresses to be excluded\nfrom being leased to DHCP clients.","The Cisco router will exclude 15 IP addresses from being leased to DHCP clients.","The Cisco router will allow only the specified IP addresses to be leased to clients.","The Cisco router will automatically create a DHCP pool using a /28 mask."],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"64","text":"To verify a Stateless DHCPv6 Client Router receiver other necessary DHPCv6 information,\nusing The show ipv6 dhcp interface-type interface-number command in global configuration\nmode of the Server Router.","options":["True","False"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"boolean"},{"sourceNumber":"65","text":"What is a method that can be used to generate an interface ID by an IPv6 host that is using\nSLAAC?","options":["ARP","DAD","EUI-64","Stateful DHCpv6"],"correctAnswers":[2],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"66","text":"Identify which message type to the order of the stateful DHCPv6 process when a client first\nconnects to an IPv6 network. DHCPv6 ADVERTISE","options":["Step 2","Step 4","Step 3","Step 1"],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"67","text":"A company implements the stateless DHCPv6 method for configuring IPv6 addresses on\nemployee workstations. After a workstation receives messages from multiple DHCPv6 servers\nto indicate their availability for DHCPv6 service, which message does it send to a server for\nconfiguration information?","options":["DHCPv6 ADVERTISE","DHCPv6 INFORMATION-REQUEST","DHCPv6 REQUEST","DHCPv6 SOLICIT"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"68","text":"What is a method that can be used to generate an interface ID by an IPv6 host that is using\nSLAAC?.","options":["ARP","random generation","DAD","Stateful DHCpv6"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"69","text":"The first step in configuring a Stateless DHCPv6 server is enabling the IPv6 routing using the\nipv6 unicast-routing command","options":["True","False"],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"boolean"},{"sourceNumber":"70","text":"Under which circumstance would a router usually be configured as a DHCPv4 client?","options":["This is an ISP requirement.","The router has a fixed IP address.","The router is meant to provide IP addresses to the hosts.","The administrator needs the router to act as a relay agent."],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"71","text":"Which DHCPv4 message will a client send to accept an IPv4 address that is offered by a DHCP\nserver?","options":["unicast DHCPREQUEST","broadcast DHCPACK","broadcast DHCPREQUEST","unicast DHCPACK"],"correctAnswers":[2],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"72","text":"A host PC is attempting to lease an address through DHCP. What message is sent by the server\nto let the client know it is able to use the provided IP information?","options":["DHCPDISCOVER","DHCPOFFER","DHCPREQUEST","DHCPACK"],"correctAnswers":[3],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"73","text":"A DHCP-enabled client PC has just booted. During which steps will the client PC use broadcast\nmessages when communicating with a DHCP server?","options":["DHCPREQUEST","DHCPNAK","DHCPACK","DHCPOFFER"],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"74","text":"Which kind of message is sent by a DHCP client when its IP address lease has expired?​","options":["a DHCPREQUEST unicast message","a DHCPDISCOVER broadcast message","a DHCPREQUEST broadcast message","a DHCPDISCOVER unicast message"],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"75","text":"To verify that the hosts have received IPv6 addressing information, use the ipconfig/all\ncommand.","options":["True","False"],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"boolean"},{"sourceNumber":"76","text":"A company uses the method SLAAC to configure IPv6 addresses for the workstations of the\nemployees. A network administrator configured the IPv6 address on the LAN interface of the\nrouter. The interface status is UP. However, the workstations on the LAN segment did not obtain\nthe correct prefix and prefix length. What else should be configured on the router that is\nattached to the LAN segment for the workstations to obtain the information?​","options":["R1(config)# ipv6 unicast-routing","R1(config)# ipv6 dhcp pool < name of the pool >","R1(config-if)# ipv6 nd other-config-flag","R1(config-if)# ipv6 enable"],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"77","text":"As a DHCPv4 client lease is about to expire, what is the message that the client sends the\nDHCP server?","options":["DHCPACK","DHCPOFFER","DHCPDISCOVER","DHCPREQUEST"],"correctAnswers":[3],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"78","text":"a message that is used to locate any available DHCP server on a network","options":["DHCPRQUEST","DHCPACK","DHCPDISCOVER","DHCPOFFER"],"correctAnswers":[2],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"79","text":"Identify which message type to the order of the stateful DHCPv6 process when a client first\nconnects to an IPv6 network. DHCPv6 Request","options":["Step 3","Step 4","Step 2","Step 1"],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"80","text":"The address pool of a DHCP server is configured with 192.168.184.0/26. The network\nadministrator reserves 18 IP addresses for access points. How many IP addresses are left in\nthe pool to be assigned to other hosts?","options":["46","44","57","54"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"81","text":"The A flag signifies that additional information is available from a stateless DHCPv6 server","options":["True","False"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"boolean"},{"sourceNumber":"82","text":"A network administrator configures a router to send RA messages with M flag as 0 and O flag\nas 1. Which statement describes the effect of this configuration when a PC tries to configure its\nIPv6 address?","options":["It should contact a DHCPv6 server for the prefix, the prefix-length information, and an interface\nID that is both random and unique.","It should contact a DHCPv6 server for all the information that it needs.","It should use the information that is contained in the RA message exclusively.","It should use the information that is contained in the RA message and contact a DHCPv6 server for\nadditional information."],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"83","text":"A Flag signifies to use SLAAC to create an IPv6 Global Unicast Address","options":["True","False"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"boolean"},{"sourceNumber":"84","text":"The O flag signifies that additional information is available from a stateless DHCPv6 server","options":["True","False"],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"boolean"},{"sourceNumber":"85","text":"The A Flag signifies to use SLAAC to create an IPv6 Global Unicast Address","options":["True","False"],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"boolean"},{"sourceNumber":"86","text":"By default, IPv6 addressing is enable in router.","options":["True","False"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"boolean"},{"sourceNumber":"87","text":"Refer to the exhibit. PC-A is unable to receive an IPv6 address from the stateful DHCPv6\nserver. What is the problem?","options":["The ipv6 dhcp relay command should use the link-local address of the DHCP server.","The ipv6 nd managed-config-flag command should be ipv6 nd other-config-flag .","The ipv6 nd managed-config-flag should be applied to interface Gig0/1.","The ipv6 dhcp relay command should be applied to interface Gig0/0."],"correctAnswers":[3],"images":["data:image/png;base64,"],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"88","text":"Which message does an IPv4 host use to reply when it receives a DHCPOFFER message from\na DHCP server?","options":["DHCPOFFER","DHCPREQUEST","DHCPDISCOVER","DHCPACK"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"89","text":"Refer to the exhibit. What protocol can be configured on gateway routers R1 and R2 that will\nallow traffic from the internal LAN to be load balanced across the two gateways to the Internet?","options":["PVST+","PVST","GLBP","STP"],"correctAnswers":[2],"images":["data:image/png;base64,"],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"90","text":"How does an IPv6 client ensure that it has a unique address after it configures its IPv6 address\nusing the SLAAC allocation method?","options":["It contacts the DHCPv6 server via a special formed ICMPv6 message.","It sends an ICMPv6 Neighbor Solicitation message with the IPv6 address as the target IPv6\naddress.","It checks with the IPv6 address database that is hosted by the SLAAC server.","It sends an ARP message with the IPv6 address as the destination IPv6 address."],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"91","text":"The client accepting the IP address provided by the DHCP server","options":["DHCPDISCOVER","DHCPACK","DHCPREQUEST","DHCPOFFER"],"correctAnswers":[2],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"92","text":"a message that is used to suggest a lease to a client","options":["DHCPOFFER","DHCPACK","DHCPDISCOVER","DHCPRQUEST"],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"93","text":"What will happen if one port in an EtherChannel is configured in VLAN22 & all other ports are\nconfigured in VLAN11?","options":["The EtherChannel bundle will stay up if either PAgP or LACP is used","The EtherChannel bundle will stay up if the ports were configured with no negotiation","The EtherChannel bundle will stay up only if LACP is used","The EtherChannel bundle will stay up only if PAgP is used"],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"94","text":"Which Cisco command will initiate EtherChannel interface configuration mode?","options":["#interface port-channel interface-identifier","#channel-group group-identifier","#interface interface-identifier","#interface range interfaced-identifier"],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"95","text":"Which is a PVST+ port state is MAC addresses learned?","options":["blocking","forwarding","listening","disabled"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"96","text":"What does a switch do when a frame is received on an interface and the destination hardware\naddress is unknown or not in the filter table?","options":["Sends back a message to the originating station asking for a name resolution","Floods the network with the frame looking for the device","Drops the frame","Forwards the switch to the first available link"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"97","text":"Which channel group mode would place an interface in a negotiating state using PAgP?","options":["desirable","active","passive","on"],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"98","text":"Which port role is assigned to the switch port that has the lowest cost to reach the root bridge?","options":["root port","disabled port","designated port","non-designated port"],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"99","text":"Refer to the exhibit. Which switch will be the root bridge after the election process is complete?","options":["S1","S3","S2","S4"],"correctAnswers":[2],"images":["data:image/png;base64,"],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"100","text":"In which port state does a switch learn MAC addresses and process BPDUs in a PVST\nnetwork?","options":["listening","learning","disabled","blocking"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"101","text":"Which switching technology would allow each access layer switch link to be aggregated to\nprovide more bandwidth between each Layer 2 switch and the Layer 3 switch?","options":["HSRP","trunking","EtherChannel","PortFast"],"correctAnswers":[2],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"102","text":"A network administrator is configuring an EtherChannel link between switches SW1 and SW2\nby using the command SW1(config-if-range)# channel-group 1 mode auto . Which command\nmust be used on SW2 to enable this EtherChannel?","options":["SW2(config-if-range)# channel-group 1 mode desirable","SW2(config-if-range)# channel-group 1 mode on","SW2(config-if-range)# channel-group 1 mode active","SW2(config-if-range)# channel-group 1 mode passive"],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"103","text":"It is the Cisco Implementation of IEEE 802.1D","options":["RAPID PVST+","MSTP","RSTP","PVST+"],"correctAnswers":[3],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"104","text":"STP is __________________.","options":["An evolution of STP that provides faster convergence","A Cisco enhancement of RSTP to provide a spanning-tree instance for each VLAN","A protocol that allows multiple VLANs to run in a single spanning-tree instance","The legacy standard for STP that runs all VLANs in a single spanning-tree instance."],"correctAnswers":[3],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"105","text":"Which statement is true about EtherChannel?","options":["A trunk port can be part of an EtherChannel bundle","EtherChannel operates only at Layer 2","PAGP cannot be used in conjunction with EtherChannel","EtherChannel can support up to a maximum of ten separate links"],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"106","text":"Which technology is an open protocol standard that allows switches to automatically bundle\nphysical ports into a single logical link?","options":["Multilink PPP","PAgP","DTP","LACP"],"correctAnswers":[3],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"107","text":"Which statement describes a spanning-tree network that has converged?","options":["All switch and bridge ports are in either the forwarding or blocking state.","All switch and bridge ports are either blocking or looping.","All switch and bridge ports are assigned as either root or designated ports.","All switch and bridge ports are in the forwarding state."],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"108","text":"Refer to the exhibit. An administrator wants to form an EtherChannel between the two switches\nby using the Port Aggregation Protocol. If switch S1 is configured to be in auto mode, which\nmode should be configured on S2 to form the EtherChannel?","options":["off","desirable","auto","on"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"109","text":"It is a Fast converging enhancement of IEEE 802.1D","options":["RAPID PVST+","MSTP","RSTP","PVST+"],"correctAnswers":[2],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"110","text":"A switch is configured to run STP. What term describes the reference point for all path\ncalculations?","options":["disabled","designated port","root port","root bridge"],"correctAnswers":[3],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"111","text":"What is the value used to determine which port on a non-root bridge will become a root port in a\nSTP network?","options":["the path cost","the VTP revision number","the lowest MAC address of all the ports in the switch","the highest MAC address of all the ports in the switch"],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"112","text":"Refer to the exhibit. A network engineer is troubleshooting host connectivity on a LAN that uses\na first hop redundancy protocol. Which IPv4 gateway address should be configured on the host?","options":["192.168.2.100","192.168.2.2","192.168.2.1","192.168.2.0"],"correctAnswers":[0],"images":["data:image/png;base64,"],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"113","text":"Refer to the exhibit. What should be done to allow PC-A to receive an IPv6 address from the\nDHCPv6 server?","options":["Add the IPv6 address 2001:DB8:1234:5678::10/64 to the interface configuration of the DHCPv6 server.","Change the ipv6 nd managed-config-flag command to ipv6 nd other-config-flag .","Add the ipv6 dhcp relay command to interface Fa0/0.","Configure the ipv6 nd managed-config-flag command on interface Fa0/1."],"correctAnswers":[2],"images":["data:image/png;base64,"],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"114","text":"A router that provided DHCPv6 forwarding services is a DHCP Relay Agent","options":["True","False"],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"boolean"},{"sourceNumber":"115","text":"ipconfig/all command can be used in Routers.","options":["True","False"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"boolean"},{"sourceNumber":"116","text":"The following configuration are used to configure stateless DHCPv6 Client on a Router.​\nR(config)# ipv6 unicast-routing​\nR(config)# interface interface-type interface-number​\nR(config-if)#ipv6 enable​\nR(config-if)#ipv6 address autoconfig","options":["True","False"],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"boolean"},{"sourceNumber":"117","text":"The second step in configuring a stateless DHCPv6 is to enable ipv6 unicast-routing command.","options":["True","False"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"boolean"},{"sourceNumber":"118","text":"The address pool of a DHCP server is configured with 10.19.44.0/24. The network administrator\nreserves 3 IP addresses for servers. How many IP addresses are left in the pool to be assigned\nto other hosts?","options":["249","255","251","241"],"correctAnswers":[2],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"119","text":"A message that is used to identify the explicit server and lease offer to accept.","options":["DHCPDISCOVER","DHCPACK","DHCPOFFER","DHCPRQUEST"],"correctAnswers":[3],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"120","text":"Refer to the exhibit. PC1 is configured to obtain a dynamic IP address from the DHCP server.\nPC1 has been shut down for two weeks. When PC1 boots and tries to request an available IP\naddress, which destination IP address will PC1 place in the IP header?","options":["192.168.1.255","192.168.1.8","192.168.1.1","255.255.255.255"],"correctAnswers":[3],"images":["data:image/png;base64,"],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"121","text":"The address pool of a DHCP server is configured with 172.21.121.0/25. The network\nadministrator reserves 12 IP addresses for web servers. How many IP addresses are left in the\npool to be assigned to other hosts?","options":["112","115","114","118"],"correctAnswers":[2],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"122","text":"Identify which message type to the order of the stateful DHCPv6 process when a client first\nconnects to an IPv6 network. DHCPv6 SOLICIT","options":["Step 4","Step 1","Step 2","Step 3"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"123","text":"The address pool of a DHCP server is configured with 192.168.234.0/27. The network\nadministrator reserves 22 IP addresses for IP phones. How many IP addresses are left in the\npool to be assigned to other hosts?","options":["10","21","18","8"],"correctAnswers":[3],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"124","text":"A DHCP server responding to the initial request by a client","options":["DHCPOFFER","DHCPDISCOVER","DHCPREQUEST","DHCPACK"],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"125","text":"The address pool of a DHCP server is configured with 172.23.143.0/26. The network\nadministrator reserves 14 IP addresses for file servers. How many IP addresses are left in the\npool to be assigned to other hosts?","options":["50","61","58","48"],"correctAnswers":[3],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"126","text":"What is used in the EUI-64 process to create an IPv6 interface ID on an IPv6 enabled interface?","options":["an IPv4 address that is configured on the interface","an IPv6 address that is provided by a DHCPv6 server","the MAC address of the IPv6 enabled interface","a randomly generated 64-bit hexadecimal address"],"correctAnswers":[2],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"127","text":"The O Flag signifies to use SLAAC to create an IPv6 Global Unicast Address","options":["True","False"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"boolean"},{"sourceNumber":"128","text":"a message that is used to acknowledge that the lease is successful","options":["DHCPOFFER","DHCPDISCOVER","DHCPACK","DHCPRQUEST"],"correctAnswers":[2],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"129","text":"When a client is requesting an initial address lease from a DHCP server, why is the\nDHCPREQUEST message sent as a broadcast?","options":["The client does not have a MAC address assigned yet, so it cannot send a unicast message at Layer 2.","The client does not yet know the IP address of the DHCP server that sent the offer.","The client may have received offers from multiple servers, and the broadcast serves to\nimplicitly decline those other offers.","The DHCP server may be on a different subnet, so the request must be sent as a broadcast."],"correctAnswers":[2],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"130","text":"Which command will allow a network administrator to check the IP address that is assigned to a\nparticular MAC address?","options":["Router# show ip dhcp pool","Router# show running-config I section_dhcp","Router# show ip dhcp server statistics","Router# show ip dhcp binding"],"correctAnswers":[3],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"131","text":"An administrator issues the commands:​\nRouter(config)# interface g0/1​\nRouter(config-if)# ip address dhcp​\nWhat is the administrator trying to achieve?","options":["configuring the router to act as a DHCPv4 server","configuring the router to act as a relay agent","configuring the router to obtain IP parameters from a DHCPv4 server","configuring the router to resolve IP address conflicts"],"correctAnswers":[2],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"132","text":"The address pool of a DHCP server is configured with 172.18.93.0/25. The network\nadministrator reserves 10 IP addresses for web servers. How many IP addresses are left in the\npool to be assigned to other hosts?","options":["114","116","106","120"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"133","text":"To verify a Stateless DHCPv6 Client Router receiver other necessary DHPCv6 information,\nusing The show ipv6 dhcp interface-type interface-number command in global configuration\nmode of the Client Router.","options":["True","False"],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"boolean"},{"sourceNumber":"134","text":"The M flag signifies to use a stateful DHCPv6 server to obtain an IPv6 Global Unicast Address.","options":["True","False"],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"boolean"},{"sourceNumber":"135","text":"Which DHCP IPv4 message contains the following information?​\nDestination address: 255.255.255.255​\nClient IPv4 address: 0.0.0.0​\nDefault gateway address: 0.0.0.0​\nSubnet mask: 0.0.0.0","options":["DHCPOFFER","DHCPREQUEST","DHCPACK","DHCPDISCOVER"],"correctAnswers":[3],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"136","text":"Which statement describes an EtherChannel implementation?","options":["EtherChannel can support up to a maximum of ten separate links.","A trunked port can be part of an EtherChannel bundle.","PAgP cannot be used in conjunction with EtherChannel.","EtherChannel operates only at Layer 2."],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"137","text":"A switch is configured to run STP. What term describes the switch port closest, in terms of\noverall cost, to the root bridge?","options":["disabled","alternate port","designated port","root port"],"correctAnswers":[3],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"138","text":"What is the function of STP in a scalable network?","options":["It combines multiple switch trunk links to act as one logical link for increased bandwidth.","It disables redundant paths to eliminate Layer 2 loops.","It protects the edge of the enterprise network from malicious activity.","It decreases the size of the failure domain to contain the impact of failures."],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"139","text":"In which circumstance are multiple copies of the same unicast frame likely to be transmitted in a\nswitched LAN?","options":["When upper-layer protocols require high reliability","In an improperly implemented redundant topology","After broken links are reestablished","During high-traffic periods"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"140","text":"A set of switches is being connected in a LAN topology. Which STP bridge priority value will\nmake it least likely for the switch to be selected as the root?","options":["4096","32768","65535","61440"],"correctAnswers":[3],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"141","text":"If you want to disable STP on a port connected to a server, which command would you use?","options":["spanning-tree security","spanning-tree portfast","spanning-tree off","disable spanning-tree"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"142","text":"A trunk link between two switches has reached its capacity. How can this be addressed in the\nmost economical way?","options":["Create additional broadcast domains by inserting a router","Combine physical ports into a high-speed logical link by configuring the EtherChannel","Increase the speed of the ports","Decrease the size of inter-switch collision domain by configuring additional VLANs"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"143","text":"Refer to the exhibit. On the basis of the output that is shown, what can be determined about the\nEtherChannel bundle?","options":["A Cisco proprietary protocol was used to negotiate the EtherChannel link.","Two Gigabit Ethernet ports are used to form the EtherChannel.","The EtherChannel bundle is operating at both Layer 2 and Layer 3.","The EtherChannel bundle is down."],"correctAnswers":[0],"images":["data:image/png;base64,"],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"144","text":"Refer to the exhibit. A network administrator is configuring a router as a DHCPv6 server. The\nadministrator issues a show ipv6 dhcp pool command to verify the configuration. Which\nstatement explains the reason that the number of active clients is 0?","options":["The IPv6 DHCP pool configuration has no IPv6 address range specified.","The state is not maintained by the DHCPv6 server under stateless DHCPv6 operation.","No clients have communicated with the DHCPv6 server yet.","The default gateway address is not provided in the pool."],"correctAnswers":[1],"images":["data:image/png;base64,"],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"145","text":"A small coffee shop is offering free Wi-Fi to customers. The network includes a wireless router\nand a DSL modem that is connected to the local phone company. What method is typically used\nto configure the connection to the phone company?","options":["Set the DSL modem as a DHCP client to get a public IP address from the wireless router.","Set the WAN connection in the wireless router as a DHCP client.","Set the connection","Set the DSL modem as a DHCP client to the phone company and a DHCP server for the internal\nconnection."],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"146","text":"What is one indication that a Windows computer did not receive an IPv4 address from a DHCP\nserver?","options":["The computer receives an IP address that starts with 169.254.","The computer cannot ping other devices on the same network with IP addresses in the 169.254.0.0/16\nrange.","The computer cannot ping 127.0.0.1.","Windows displays a DHCP timeout message."],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"147","text":"A client initiating a message to find a DHCP server.","options":["DHCPACK","DHCPREQUEST","DHCPDISCOVER","DHCPOFFER"],"correctAnswers":[2],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"148","text":"Refer to the exhibit. A network administrator is configuring a router for DHCPv6 operation.\nWhich conclusion can be drawn based on the commands?","options":["The router is configured for stateful DHCPv6 operation, but the DHCP pool configuration is incomplete.","Clients would configure the interface IDs above 0010.","The router is configured for stateless DHCPv6 operation.","The DHCPv6 server name is ACAD_CLASS."],"correctAnswers":[2],"images":["data:image/png;base64,"],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"149","text":"SLAAC is a service which means there is no server that maintains network address information\nto know which IPv6 addresses are being used and which ones are available.","options":["True","False"],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"boolean"},{"sourceNumber":"150","text":"Identify which message type to the order of the stateful DHCPv6 process when a client first\nconnects to an IPv6 network. DHCPv6 REPLY","options":["Step 3","Step 4","Step 2","Step 1"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"151","text":"Which statement is true about DHCP operation?​","options":["If the client receives several DHCPOFFER messages from different servers, it sends a unicast\nDHCPREQUEST message to the server from which it chooses to obtain the IP information.","The DHCPDISCOVER message contains the IP address and subnet mask to be assigned, the IP\naddress of the DNS server, and the IP address of the default gateway.","A client must wait for lease expiration before it sends another DHCPREQUEST message.","When a device that is configured to use DHCP boots, the client broadcasts a\nDHCPDISCOVER message to identify any available DHCP servers on the network."],"correctAnswers":[3],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"152","text":"What is an advantage of configuring a Cisco router as a relay agent?","options":["It reduces the response time from a DHCP server.","It can forward both broadcast and multicast messages on behalf of clients.","It will allow DHCPDISCOVER messages to pass without alteration.","It can provide relay services for multiple UDP services."],"correctAnswers":[3],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"153","text":"Refer to the exhibit. Based on the output that is shown, what kind of IPv6 addressing is being\nconfigured?","options":["static link-local","stateful DHCPv6","SLAAC","stateless DHCPv6"],"correctAnswers":[3],"images":["data:image/png;base64,"],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"154","text":"A company uses the SLAAC method to configure IPv6 addresses for the employee\nworkstations. Which address will a client use as its default gateway?​","options":["the link-local address of the router interface that is attached to the network","the global unicast address of the router interface that is attached to the network","the unique local address of the router interface that is attached to the network","the all-routers multicast address"],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"155","text":"To enable SLAAC, it should have the following: Link-local IPv6 address, Global Unicast address\n/ subnet and IPv6 all-nodes group.","options":["True","False"],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"boolean"},{"sourceNumber":"156","text":"Refer to the exhibit. A network administrator is configuring an EtherChannel link between two\nswitches, SW1 and SW2. Which statement describes the effect after the commands are issued\non SW1 and SW2?","options":["The EtherChannel is established without negotiation.","The EtherChannel is established after SW1 initiates the link request.","The EtherChannel fails to establish.","The EtherChannel is established after SW2 initiates the link request."],"correctAnswers":[2],"images":["data:image/png;base64,"],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"157","text":"Which statement is true regarding the Port Aggregation Protocol?","options":["Configuration changes made on the port-channel interface apply to all physical ports assigned\nto the port-channel interface.","Configuration changes made on a physical port that is a member of a port-channel interface apply to\nthe port- channel interface.","Configuration changes are not permitted with Port Aggregation Protocol; instead, the standardised Link\nAggregation Control Protocol should be used if configuration changes are required.","The physical port must first be disassociated from the port-channel interface before any configuration\nchanges can be made."],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"158","text":"Which of the following statement is true?","options":["A switch creates a single collision domain and a single broadcast domain. A router creates a single\ncollision domain.","A switch creates a single collision domain and separate broadcast domains. A router provides a\nseparate broadcast domain as well.","A switch creates separate collision domains and separate broadcast domains. A router provides\nseparate collision domains.","A switch creates separate collision domains but one broadcast domain. A router provides a\nseparate broadcast domain."],"correctAnswers":[3],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"159","text":"Which statement best describes implementing a Layer 3 EtherChannel?","options":["A Layer 3 address is assigned to the channel-group interface.","EtherChannel is a Layer 2 and not a Layer 3 feature.","Implementation requires switchport mode trunk and matching parameters","Implementation requires disabling switchport mode."],"correctAnswers":[3],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"160","text":"After an EtherChannel is configured between two Cisco switches, interface port-channel 1 is in\nthe down/down state.​\nSwitch A is configured with channel-group 1 mode active, while Switch B is configured with\nchannel-group 1 mode desirable.​\nWhy is the EtherChannel bundle not working?","options":["The switch ports are not configured in trunking mode.","LACP priority must be configured on both switches.","The switches are using mismatched EtherChannel negotiation modes.","The channel group identifier must be different for Switch A and Switch B."],"correctAnswers":[2],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"161","text":"Which protocol is a link aggregation protocol?","options":["RSTP","STP","EtherChannel","PAgP"],"correctAnswers":[3],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"162","text":"An administrator wants to configure hosts to automatically assign IPv6 addresses to themselves\nby the use of Router Advertisement messages, but also to obtain the DNS server address from\na DHCPv6 server. Which address assignment method should be configured?","options":["SLAAC","stateless DHCPv6","RA and EUI-64","stateful DHCPv6"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"163","text":"What is the reason that an ISP commonly assigns a DHCP address to a wireless router in a\nSOHO environment?","options":["easy configuration on ISP firewall","easy IP address management","better network performance","better connectivity"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"164","text":"Refer to the exhibit. Which destination MAC address is used when frames are sent from the\nworkstation to the default gateway?","options":["MAC address of the standby router","MAC addresses of both the forwarding and standby routers","MAC address of the forwarding router","MAC address of the virtual router"],"correctAnswers":[3],"images":["data:image/png;base64,"],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"165","text":"By default, an IPv6-enabled router periodically send ICMPv6 RAs which simplifies how a host\ncan dynamically create or acquire its IPv6 configuration","options":["True","False"],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"boolean"},{"sourceNumber":"166","text":"The address pool of a DHCP server is configured with 10.92.71.0/25. The network administrator\nreserves 8 IP addresses for servers. How many IP addresses are left in the pool to be assigned\nto other hosts?","options":["116","108","118","119"],"correctAnswers":[2],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"167","text":"The address pool of a DHCP server is configured with 10.3.2.0/24. The network administrator\nreserves 3 IP addresses for printers. How many IP addresses are left in the pool to be assigned\nto other hosts?","options":["251","249","252","241"],"correctAnswers":[0],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"168","text":"A router that provides DHCPv6 forwarding services is a DHCP Server.","options":["True","False"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"boolean"},{"sourceNumber":"169","text":"What does the command channel-group 1 mode desirable do?​\nInterface FastEthernet 0/13​\nChannel-group 1 mode desirable","options":["enables PAgP only if a PAgP device is detected","enables EtherChannel only","enables LACP only if a LACP device is detected","enables PAgP unconditionally"],"correctAnswers":[3],"type":"choice"},{"sourceNumber":"170","text":"What is the status of port-channel if LACP is misconfigured?","options":["Errdisabled","Disabled","Enabled","Forwarding"],"correctAnswers":[1],"type":"choice"}],"source":"S2 It0015 - Clean Reviewer.pdf"};
